# Build context: ./backend (docker-compose.yml, service `backend`).
# This is the file Docker actually reads for that build -- the repo-root
# .dockerignore does NOT apply to a subdirectory context.
#
# Patterns are matched against the path relative to the context root and `*`
# does not cross `/`, so anything that can appear at any depth needs the `**/`
# prefix. Verified: without it, backend/app/__pycache__/*.pyc still shipped.
#
# Keep in sync with sync/.dockerignore.

# The recipe itself: never needed inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Secrets / local state. None of these are committed, but an image layer is a
# permanent, shippable copy -- exclude them before they can exist.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.credentials
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Python build/test artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml

# Tests do not run inside the runtime image; CI runs them from the repo root.
**/tests
**/test_*.py
**/conftest.py

# Editor / OS noise
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
